---
// FirstClub · Taste Passport case study. Self-contained FirstClub identity
// (Fraunces + Poppins, cream/green/gold) — intentionally its own look, not the
// portfolio's Manrope/DM Mono chrome. Served at /work/taste-passport; images in
// /public/taste-passport/. Discoverable via a card in the homepage Work grid.
const canonical = 'https://jitesht.com/work/taste-passport';
const description =
  'FirstClub Taste Passport — a seasonal, deterministic stamp-collection concept (no chance mechanics) built entirely on FirstClub’s live design system.';
const figmaUrl =
  'https://www.figma.com/design/CAbVYp5Gu2sIuiLeOP4nM3/Untitled?node-id=9-203&t=Sg7YTfYD3RNLsSag-1';
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>FirstClub · Taste Passport — Case Study</title>
<meta name="description" content={description}>
<link rel="canonical" href={canonical}>
<meta name="author" content="Jitesh Thakker">
<meta property="og:type" content="article">
<meta property="og:title" content="FirstClub · Taste Passport — Case Study">
<meta property="og:description" content={description}>
<meta property="og:url" content={canonical}>
<meta property="og:image" content="https://jitesht.com/taste-passport/fc05.png">
<meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Fraunces:opsz,wght@9..144,400;9..144,500;9..144,600;9..144,700&family=Poppins:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
<style is:global>
  :root{
    --cream:#F7F2E7; --paper:#F1E9D6; --blush:#F3EBDD;
    --g900:#173F29; --g700:#1E5C3F; --sage:#DCEBD7; --lime:#EFF3D9;
    --gold:#DFA84D; --gold-deep:#B9862E;
    --ink:#1D1B16; --ink-soft:#6B6558; --ink-faint:#9C9686; --line:#E4DCC8;
    --crimson:#C4485C;
  }
  *{box-sizing:border-box;margin:0;padding:0}
  html{scroll-behavior:smooth}
  body{background:var(--cream);color:var(--ink);font-family:'Poppins',system-ui,sans-serif;line-height:1.55}
  .serif{font-family:'Fraunces',Georgia,serif}
  img{display:block;max-width:100%;height:auto}

  /* ===== nav ===== */
  .toc{position:sticky;top:0;z-index:50;background:rgba(247,242,231,.92);backdrop-filter:blur(8px);border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}
  .toc-inner{max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;padding:14px 28px;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:22px;overflow-x:auto;scrollbar-width:none}
  .toc-inner::-webkit-scrollbar{display:none}
  .toc-brand{font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-weight:600;font-size:15px;color:var(--g900);flex:none;white-space:nowrap}
  .toc a{font-size:12.5px;color:var(--ink-soft);text-decoration:none;font-weight:500;white-space:nowrap;flex:none}
  .toc a:hover{color:var(--g700)}

  /* ===== hero ===== */
  .hero{padding:88px 28px 76px;background:linear-gradient(180deg,#EAF0DE 0%,var(--cream) 78%);text-align:center}
  .hero .kick{font-size:11.5px;letter-spacing:.22em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--g700);font-weight:600}
  .hero h1{font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-weight:600;font-size:clamp(34px,6vw,58px);line-height:1.06;color:var(--g900);margin-top:16px;max-width:16ch;margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto}
  .hero .dek{font-size:16px;color:var(--ink-soft);max-width:52ch;margin:20px auto 0;line-height:1.6}
  .hero .meta{margin-top:30px;display:flex;justify-content:center;gap:26px;flex-wrap:wrap}
  .hero .meta div{font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--ink-faint);font-weight:600}
  .hero .meta div b{display:block;font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:15px;color:var(--ink);text-transform:none;letter-spacing:0;margin-top:3px;font-weight:600}

  /* external-link button (View in Figma) — FirstClub pill */
  .fig-cta{margin-top:30px;display:flex;justify-content:center}
  .fig-btn{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:9px;background:var(--g900);color:#fff;font-family:'Poppins',sans-serif;font-weight:600;font-size:13.5px;text-decoration:none;padding:12px 22px;border-radius:30px;border:1px solid var(--g900);transition:background .18s,transform .18s}
  .fig-btn:hover{background:var(--g700);transform:translateY(-1px)}
  .fig-btn svg{flex:none}
  .fig-foot{display:flex;justify-content:center;margin-bottom:20px}
  .backlink{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;font-family:'Poppins',sans-serif;font-size:12.5px;font-weight:600;color:var(--g700);text-decoration:none;flex:none;white-space:nowrap}
  .backlink:hover{color:var(--g900)}

  /* ===== sections ===== */
  section{max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;padding:64px 28px}
  section + section{border-top:1px solid var(--line)}
  .s-kick{font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.2em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--g700);font-weight:600;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px}
  .s-kick::before{content:"";width:20px;height:1.5px;background:var(--g700);border-radius:2px}
  .s-title{font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-weight:600;font-size:clamp(24px,3.4vw,34px);color:var(--ink);margin-top:12px;max-width:22ch}
  .s-body{font-size:14.5px;color:var(--ink-soft);max-width:62ch;margin-top:14px;line-height:1.7}
  .s-body strong{color:var(--ink);font-weight:600}

  /* ===== entry point cards (intro section) ===== */
  .ep-grid{margin-top:40px;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:20px}
  .ep-card{background:var(--paper);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:20px;padding:26px 22px}
  .ep-num{width:30px;height:30px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--g900);color:var(--gold);font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-weight:600;font-size:14px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center}
  .ep-card h3{font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-weight:600;font-size:17px;margin-top:14px;color:var(--g900)}
  .ep-card p{font-size:12.5px;color:var(--ink-soft);margin-top:8px;line-height:1.6}
  .ep-tag{display:inline-block;margin-top:12px;font-size:10px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--g700);background:var(--sage);padding:4px 10px;border-radius:20px}

  /* ===== screen block ===== */
  .flow-group{margin-top:50px}
  .flow-group:first-of-type{margin-top:44px}
  .fg-head{display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;margin-bottom:26px;flex-wrap:wrap}
  .fg-head .fg-n{font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-weight:600;font-size:13px;color:var(--gold-deep);background:var(--blush);border:1px solid var(--line);width:28px;height:28px;border-radius:50%;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;flex:none}
  .fg-head h3{font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-weight:600;font-size:20px;color:var(--ink)}
  .fg-head .fg-sub{font-size:12.5px;color:var(--ink-faint)}

  .shots{display:flex;gap:26px;overflow-x:auto;padding:6px 2px 16px;scroll-snap-type:x proximity}
  .shots::-webkit-scrollbar{height:6px}
  .shots::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb{background:var(--line);border-radius:10px}
  .shot{flex:0 0 auto;width:230px;scroll-snap-align:start}
  .shot .frame{border-radius:20px;overflow:hidden;box-shadow:0 16px 34px -18px rgba(20,40,25,.35);border:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,.05)}
  .shot .frame img{width:100%}
  .shot .cap{margin-top:13px}
  .shot .cap .t{font-size:12.5px;font-weight:600;color:var(--ink)}
  .shot .cap .d{font-size:11.5px;color:var(--ink-soft);margin-top:4px;line-height:1.55}

  .why{margin-top:22px;background:var(--sage);border-radius:16px;padding:18px 20px;display:flex;gap:12px;align-items:flex-start}
  .why svg{flex:none;color:var(--g700);margin-top:2px}
  .why p{font-size:12.5px;color:var(--g900);line-height:1.6}
  .why p b{font-weight:600}

  .note-strip{margin-top:22px;background:var(--lime);border-radius:16px;padding:16px 20px;font-size:12.5px;color:var(--ink-soft);line-height:1.6}
  .note-strip b{color:var(--ink)}

  /* ===== rules grid ===== */
  .rules{margin-top:36px;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:16px}
  .rule{border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:16px;padding:18px 20px;background:var(--cream)}
  .rule .rt{font-size:13.5px;font-weight:600;color:var(--g900);display:flex;align-items:center;gap:9px}
  .rule .rt svg{color:var(--g700);flex:none}
  .rule p{font-size:12px;color:var(--ink-soft);margin-top:7px;line-height:1.6}

  /* ===== decision log ===== */
  .dl{margin-top:36px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:14px}
  .dl-row{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1.4fr;gap:22px;padding:18px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}
  .dl-row:last-child{border-bottom:none}
  .dl-q{font-size:13px;font-weight:600;color:var(--ink)}
  .dl-a{font-size:12.5px;color:var(--ink-soft);line-height:1.6}
  .dl-a b{color:var(--g700);font-weight:600}

  /* ===== closing ===== */
  .close{background:linear-gradient(160deg,#2C6B47,#123A26);color:#fff;text-align:center;border-top:none}
  .close .s-title{color:#fff;margin:0 auto;max-width:20ch}
  .close .s-body{color:rgba(255,255,255,.78);margin:14px auto 0}
  .close .s-kick{color:var(--gold-soft,#F1DCA6);justify-content:center}
  .close .s-kick::before{background:var(--gold)}

  footer{padding:34px 28px;text-align:center;font-size:11.5px;color:var(--ink-faint)}

  @media (max-width:820px){
    .ep-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}
    .rules{grid-template-columns:1fr}
    .dl-row{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:6px}
    .hero{padding:64px 22px 52px}
    section{padding:48px 20px}
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<nav class="toc">
  <div class="toc-inner">
    <a class="backlink" href="/">&larr; Portfolio</a>
    <span class="toc-brand serif">Taste Passport</span>
    <a href="#entry">Entry points</a>
    <a href="#flow-1">Order confirmed</a>
    <a href="#flow-2">Onboarding</a>
    <a href="#flow-3">The passport</a>
    <a href="#flow-4">Reward</a>
    <a href="#flow-5">Seasons</a>
    <a href="#flow-6">Persistent access</a>
    <a href="#rules">Design rules</a>
    <a href="#decisions">Key decisions</a>
  </div>
</nav>

<header class="hero">
  <div class="kick">FirstClub · Gamification concept</div>
  <h1 class="serif">The Taste Passport</h1>
  <p class="dek">A seasonal collectible built on FirstClub's existing screens and design language — turning genuine product discovery into a calm, premium ritual instead of a spin-wheel promotion.</p>
  <div class="meta">
    <div>Screens<b>12</b></div>
    <div>Entry points<b>3</b></div>
    <div>Chance mechanics<b>0</b></div>
    <div>Design system<b>FirstClub native</b></div>
  </div>
  <div class="fig-cta">
    <a class="fig-btn" href={figmaUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
      <svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M7 2h10M7 2a3 3 0 0 0 0 6m0-6v6m10-6a3 3 0 0 1 0 6H7m10 0a3 3 0 1 1-6 0m-4 0a3 3 0 0 0 0 6m0-6h4m-4 6a3 3 0 1 0 6 0v-6"/></svg>
      View in Figma
    </a>
  </div>
</header>

<section id="entry">
  <div class="s-kick">Why this exists</div>
  <h2 class="s-title">Reward discovery, not luck</h2>
  <p class="s-body">FirstClub users order in large, infrequent baskets — not daily small orders. Instead of borrowing generic spin-wheel or loot-box mechanics common in quick-commerce apps, the Taste Passport rewards genuine exploration: ordering curated, verified, or first-time-try products. Every qualifying order moves the user forward. <strong>There is no losing.</strong></p>

  <div class="ep-grid">
    <div class="ep-card">
      <div class="ep-num">1</div>
      <h3 class="serif">The passive signal</h3>
      <p>Right after an order is confirmed — the calmest, most singular moment in the whole app — a quiet reveal shows a stamp was earned. No popup, no animation competing with delivery info.</p>
      <span class="ep-tag">Order confirmed screen</span>
    </div>
    <div class="ep-card">
      <div class="ep-num">2</div>
      <h3 class="serif">The real moment</h3>
      <p>Tapping through opens the Passport itself — a collectible journal where the stamp lands, progress is visible, and a completed season unlocks a curated reward.</p>
      <span class="ep-tag">The Passport</span>
    </div>
    <div class="ep-card">
      <div class="ep-num">3</div>
      <h3 class="serif">The persistent anchor</h3>
      <p>Always available from Account Profile — never a home-screen banner. Users can check progress anytime without needing to have just placed an order.</p>
      <span class="ep-tag">Account Profile</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="flow-1">
  <div class="flow-group">
    <div class="fg-head">
      <span class="fg-n serif">1</span>
      <h3 class="serif">Entry point — order confirmation</h3>
      <span class="fg-sub">Where the stamp is quietly revealed</span>
    </div>
    <div class="shots">
      <div class="shot">
        <div class="frame"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="/taste-passport/fc01.png" alt="Order confirmed, default state"></div>
        <div class="cap"><div class="t">Default state</div><div class="d">FirstClub's existing screen, untouched. On a normal order with no qualifying find, nothing extra renders here — the passport never intrudes on delivery info.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="shot">
        <div class="frame"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="/taste-passport/fc02.png" alt="Order confirmed with stamp reveal"></div>
        <div class="cap"><div class="t">Reveal state</div><div class="d">Same screen, same calm layout. A 3-step reveal — confirmed, spotted, stamp earned — appears where the address card would sit, ending in a tap-through pill.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="shot">
        <div class="frame"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="/taste-passport/fc03.png" alt="Out for delivery map tracking, untouched"></div>
        <div class="cap"><div class="t">Out for delivery</div><div class="d">FirstClub's real live-tracking screen — deliberately left untouched. The passport signal already happened upstream, so this stays focused on one job.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="why">
      <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M12 8v4M12 16h.01"/></svg>
      <p><b>Why here, not the map screen:</b> the confirmation screen is already the quietest, most single-focus moment in the app — huge whitespace, one thing to look at. Placing the reveal here means the busier tracking screen never has to compete for attention.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="flow-2">
  <div class="flow-group">
    <div class="fg-head">
      <span class="fg-n serif">2</span>
      <h3 class="serif">First-time onboarding</h3>
      <span class="fg-sub">Shown once, before the passport is opened for the first time</span>
    </div>
    <div class="shots">
      <div class="shot">
        <div class="frame"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="/taste-passport/fc05.png" alt="Introducing Taste Passport splash"></div>
        <div class="cap"><div class="t">Introducing Taste Passport</div><div class="d">Gold emblem, holder name, and current progress — sets the tone as a keepsake, not a game screen.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="shot">
        <div class="frame"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="/taste-passport/fc06.png" alt="How Taste Passport unfolds explainer"></div>
        <div class="cap"><div class="t">How it unfolds</div><div class="d">One plain-language rule: an order leads to a stamp, stamps build collections, completed collections open one curated reward.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="flow-3">
  <div class="flow-group">
    <div class="fg-head">
      <span class="fg-n serif">3</span>
      <h3 class="serif">The Passport interior</h3>
      <span class="fg-sub">Where stamps live and progress is always visible</span>
    </div>
    <div class="shots">
      <div class="shot">
        <div class="frame"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="/taste-passport/fc07.png" alt="Passport interior, Season 1 collected finds"></div>
        <div class="cap"><div class="t">Season 1: Artisan Harvest</div><div class="d">Filled stamps show what was found (Wine Bar, Bakery, Roastery); empty slots read "Awaiting" — never a failure state, just a placeholder.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="shot">
        <div class="frame"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="/taste-passport/fc08.png" alt="Stamp detail view for Kalyani Malbec Reserve"></div>
        <div class="cap"><div class="t">Stamp detail</div><div class="d">Tapping a filled stamp shows what was collected, from which order, and why it qualified. Empty slots are intentionally not tappable — the passport is earned by ordering, not browsing.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="why">
      <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M12 8v4M12 16h.01"/></svg>
      <p><b>Deliberate constraint:</b> tapping an empty "Awaiting" slot does nothing — no preview, no shortcut to the order page. That keeps the mechanic honest to "discovery, not a promotion."</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="flow-4">
  <div class="flow-group">
    <div class="fg-head">
      <span class="fg-n serif">4</span>
      <h3 class="serif">The reward</h3>
      <span class="fg-sub">Locked → unlocked → claimed → in the cart</span>
    </div>
    <div class="shots">
      <div class="shot">
        <div class="frame"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="/taste-passport/fc09.png" alt="Locked reward state"></div>
        <div class="cap"><div class="t">Locked</div><div class="d">"3 more finds to unlock" — the reward is named and described up front, so the goal is never a mystery.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="shot">
        <div class="frame"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="/taste-passport/fc10.png" alt="Unlocked reward state"></div>
        <div class="cap"><div class="t">Unlocked</div><div class="d">Seal breaks open. Copy explains exactly what happens next before the user even taps Claim.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="shot">
        <div class="frame"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="/taste-passport/fc12.png" alt="Reward claimed and added to cart confirmation"></div>
        <div class="cap"><div class="t">Claimed</div><div class="d">Gift drops straight into the cart as a free line item — "View Cart" is the primary action, with a quiet way back to the passport for anyone not checking out yet.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="flow-5">
  <div class="flow-group">
    <div class="fg-head">
      <span class="fg-n serif">5</span>
      <h3 class="serif">Seasons &amp; archive</h3>
      <span class="fg-sub">What makes this a long-term system, not a one-off promotion</span>
    </div>
    <div class="shots">
      <div class="shot">
        <div class="frame"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="/taste-passport/fc11.png" alt="Season 2 between-seasons state with archive"></div>
        <div class="cap"><div class="t">Season 2 · Between seasons</div><div class="d">"Starts in 18 days" — anticipation, not disappointment. Past seasons live below in an archive, so completed passports are kept, not deleted.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="why">
      <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M12 8v4M12 16h.01"/></svg>
      <p><b>This is the strategic core of the concept:</b> one persistent passport, seasonal editions that complete and archive, and a between-seasons state that reads as a pause, not an ending. It's what makes this a membership relationship rather than a promotional campaign — the reason to keep coming back next season, not just this one.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="flow-6">
  <div class="flow-group">
    <div class="fg-head">
      <span class="fg-n serif">6</span>
      <h3 class="serif">Persistent access point</h3>
      <span class="fg-sub">Always reachable, never intrusive</span>
    </div>
    <div class="shots">
      <div class="shot">
        <div class="frame"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="/taste-passport/fc04.png" alt="Account Profile with Taste Passport row"></div>
        <div class="cap"><div class="t">Account Profile</div><div class="d">A quiet row — "Taste Passport 5/8" — styled identically to Addresses and Help &amp; Support. Live progress at a glance, no home-screen banner ever.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="rules">
  <div class="s-kick">Constraints held throughout</div>
  <h2 class="s-title">The rules that keep this premium</h2>
  <div class="rules">
    <div class="rule">
      <div class="rt"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M12 8v4M12 16h.01"/></svg>Deterministic only</div>
      <p>No spin wheels, scratch cards, or chance mechanics. Every qualifying order earns exactly what it earns.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="rule">
      <div class="rt"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="3" y="4" width="18" height="16" rx="2"/><path d="M3 10h18"/></svg>No home banner</div>
      <p>Gamification never competes with the primary shopping flow — access is passive (checkout) or intentional (profile) only.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="rule">
      <div class="rt"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 2l2.9 6.3 6.9.7-5.1 4.6 1.4 6.8L12 17.8 5.9 20.4l1.4-6.8L2.2 9l6.9-.7z"/></svg>Structurally can't lose</div>
      <p>There's no failed attempt state. An order either adds a stamp or it doesn't — never a penalty.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="rule">
      <div class="rt"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M4 19.5A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 6.5 17H20"/><path d="M6.5 2H20v20H6.5A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 4 19.5v-15A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 6.5 2z"/></svg>FirstClub's own system</div>
      <p>Same fonts, same pill shapes, same greens and creams as the live app — this reads as a feature, not a reskin.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="decisions">
  <div class="s-kick">Product reasoning</div>
  <h2 class="s-title">Key decisions, and why</h2>
  <div class="dl">
    <div class="dl-row">
      <div class="dl-q">Where does the stamp reveal live?</div>
      <div class="dl-a">On the <b>order-confirmed</b> screen, not the busier out-for-delivery map screen — it's already the calmest moment in the app, so nothing new needs to compete for attention.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="dl-row">
      <div class="dl-q">What happens on a zero-stamp order?</div>
      <div class="dl-a">Nothing renders. The screen stays exactly as FirstClub's existing confirmation screen — <b>no passport content appears unless a stamp was actually earned.</b></div>
    </div>
    <div class="dl-row">
      <div class="dl-q">Can users tap an empty "Awaiting" slot?</div>
      <div class="dl-a"><b>No, deliberately.</b> No preview, no shortcut to browse or order. The passport is earned by ordering, not by poking around the app.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="dl-row">
      <div class="dl-q">What happens after Claim Reward?</div>
      <div class="dl-a">The reward drops into the cart as a <b>free gift line item</b> automatically — confirmation screen offers "View Cart" as the primary action.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="dl-row">
      <div class="dl-q">What happens when a season ends?</div>
      <div class="dl-a">The passport shows <b>anticipation, not disappointment</b> — "Starts in 18 days" — while the finished passport moves into a permanent archive below.</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="close">
  <div class="s-kick">In short</div>
  <h2 class="s-title serif">A membership, not a promotion</h2>
  <p class="s-body">The Taste Passport turns FirstClub's existing quality-first identity into a quiet, collectible ritual — built entirely from screens and patterns the app already has, extended just far enough to feel new.</p>
</section>

